		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " A `this is T` predicate's type runs on to the right, as a function type's return",
			"start": 20,
			"end": 103
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " does, so a predicate keeps its pair wherever a token follows it",
			"start": 105,
			"end": 171
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " A union or intersection member, a conditional's check type, an optional element",
			"start": 379,
			"end": 461
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " A last member and an operator's operand take the pair a function type takes there,",
			"start": 621,
			"end": 706
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " written or not: bare, they read alike only where nothing follows the whole type",
